The most iconic scene in ‘Miami Vice’ (1984) is the mesmerizing night-drive sequence from the pilot episode, set to Phil Collins’ “In the Air Tonight”. It features detectives Sonny Crockett and Ricardo Tubbs silently navigating the neon-lit streets of Miami in a sleek black Ferrari, heading toward an intense, life-threatening confrontation.

